---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import ProfileAvatar from '@/components/ProfileAvatar.astro';
import { SocialLinks } from '@/components/SocialLinks';
---

<Base
  title="About - Lyes Tarzalt"
  description="Lyes Tarzalt - Product engineer based in Malaysia, originally from Algeria."
>
  <section class="max-w-lg pt-12 sm:pt-16">
    <ProfileAvatar
      class="mb-8 size-20 ring-2 ring-primary/20 ring-offset-2 ring-offset-background"
    />

    <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl font-normal tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">About</h1>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.8] text-muted-foreground">
      <p>
        I'm Lyes. Based in <span class="text-foreground">Malaysia</span>, originally from <span
          class="text-foreground">Algeria</span
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        I like building things that help people. When I see a problem, I want to understand why it
        exists before I start writing code. Most of the time the fix people ask for isn't the fix
        they need.
      </p>
      <p>
        I run the AI side of things where I work. I sit with clients, learn how their business
        actually runs, then figure out where an LLM can take boring, repetitive stuff off someone's
        plate. We once outsourced a voice agent to a third party. The result was slow and the
        architecture didn't make sense to me, so I couldn't help myself and built a better version
        on my own time. Our proposal was the last one the client saw, and honestly it wasn't great
        on paper, but the demo alone got us the deal.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of work I make tools I wish existed. <span class="text-foreground">X-Dispatch</span>
        because X-Plane had no way to browse airports on a map. <span class="text-foreground"
          >Dinar Échange</span
        > because a friend wanted an easy way to understand currency exchange rates for the Algerian dinar.
      </p>
      <p>
        I think about the whole thing. The architecture, the code, how it looks, how it feels to
        use. If someone opens the app and has to think about where to click, I messed up.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 flex items-center gap-4">
      <div class="h-px flex-1 bg-border"></div>
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.5rem] uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-muted-foreground/60">
        Elsewhere
      </span>
      <div class="h-px flex-1 bg-border"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8">
      <SocialLinks client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
